usage: nvcflow.py [-h] [--clang CLANG] [--standard {c11,c17,gnu11,gnu17}]
                  [--compiler-arg COMPILER_ARG]
                  [--token-contract {opaque,no-token-observation,preprocessed}]
                  [--max-variants MAX_VARIANTS] [--max-passes MAX_PASSES]
                  [--frontend-seconds FRONTEND_SECONDS]
                  [--frontend-memory-mib FRONTEND_MEMORY_MIB]
                  [--ast-mib AST_MIB] [--variant VARIANT] [--output OUTPUT]
                  [--audit AUDIT] [--portfolio PORTFOLIO] [--list-variants]
                  [--run-manifest] [--verifier VERIFIER]
                  [--run-target RUN_TARGET] [--run-contract RUN_CONTRACT]
                  [--codec CODEC] [--max-bytes MAX_BYTES]
                  input

Generate audited, type-checked C expression portfolios with an optional Clang.
This is a deliberately bounded set of local C rewrites, not a general theorem
prover. Identity is always retained. A run manifest can compare every
candidate after compilation, whole-file packing, and the user's execution
verifier.

positional arguments:
  input

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --clang CLANG
  --standard {c11,c17,gnu11,gnu17}
  --compiler-arg COMPILER_ARG
  --token-contract {opaque,no-token-observation,preprocessed}
  --max-variants MAX_VARIANTS
  --max-passes MAX_PASSES
  --frontend-seconds FRONTEND_SECONDS
  --frontend-memory-mib FRONTEND_MEMORY_MIB
  --ast-mib AST_MIB
  --variant VARIANT     explicit candidate ID; defaults to c-all when
                        available, otherwise raw
  --output OUTPUT
  --audit AUDIT
  --portfolio PORTFOLIO
  --list-variants
  --run-manifest        write a standalone C run manifest inside --portfolio;
                        generation does not execute it
  --verifier VERIFIER   self-contained Python checker accepting one candidate
                        binary path
  --run-target RUN_TARGET
                        explicit target triple for native packing
  --run-contract RUN_CONTRACT
                        application domain/observable contract and packing
                        non-observation assertion
  --codec CODEC         manifest codec ID; defaults to gzip-9 and xz-6
  --max-bytes MAX_BYTES
